4, 7, 11, 13, 19, 25, 26, 30-34, 38, 47, 51, 56, 57,
 <COL N="LXXXVIIIB"></COL> 68, 83, 89, 92, 97, 98. Lib. IX (c. 1-82); c. 1-4,
12, 13, 18, 19, 26, 27, 30, 31, 35, 40, 41, 45-52,
57, 58, 62, 63, 65, 69, 70, 73, 75, 76, 79-81. Lib.
X (c. 1-68); c. 1, 5, 7, 9, 11, 14, 18, 20, 25, 27,
28, 30, 34, 36, 45, 48, 49, 51, 53, 55, 56, 62-64,
66-69. Lib. XI (c. 1-78); c. 2-9, 13, 15, 18, 25-27,
30, 45, 47, 50. Lib. XII (c. 1-39); c. 11, 12, 19, 20.
Lib. XIII (c. 1-28); c. 1-3, 6, 8-10, 11-15, 18, 21,
24, 27, 28. Lib. XIV (c. 1-17); c. 1-13, 17. Lib. XV
(c. 1-44); c. 2, 3, 5-11, 13, 15-19, 24, 30, 32-36,
44. Lib. XVI (c. 1-37); c. 1, 8, 9, 11-13, 15-17, 19-24,
27, 31, 33-37.</NOTE>  decreto desumpta est, in quo ne apicem
quidem auctor mutavit. Codex vero mutilus est, et
liber decimus sextus omnino desideratur.</P> <P COM="LXXXVIIA">Multo minus antecessores suos imitatus est auctor
collectionis quae in bibliothecae Sanctae Genovefae
codice Parisiis exstat, et ex Burchardi et
Pseudo-Ivonis decreto compilata est. In quatuor
partes tota dividitur, quarum singulae in plures libros
distribuuntur <NOTE N="(304)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="LXXXVIIIB" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="LXXXVIIIB"></COL> P. I, lib. II, De sacramento baptismatis, c.
1-105. Lib. III, De sacramento altaris c. 1-153. Lib.
IV, De ecclesiis, c. 1-96. P. II, lib. I, De episcopis,
c. 1-217. Lib. II, De clericis, c. 1-217. Lib. III,
De judicibus, c. 1-67. Lib. IV, De conjugiis, c. 1-101.
Lib. V, De Deo dicatis et de jejunio, c. 1-116.
P. III, lib. I, De homicidiis, c. 1-46. Lib. II, De auguriis,
 <COL N="LXXXVIIIC"></COL> c. 1-61. Lib. III, De perjurio, c. 1-27. Lib.
IV, De ebrietate, c. 1-16. Lib. V, De fornicatione,
P. IV, lib. I, De excommunicatione, Lib. II, De confessione,
c. 1-24. Lib. III, De poenitentia, c. 1-168.
Dolendum sane est quod et hic codex mancus sit.
Praeter lib. V. P. III et lib. I. P. IV capitula, liber
primus cum rubrica et capitibus deest. Quoad reliqua
collectionem integram exhibet.</NOTE> . Non raro auctor libros eodem
 <COL N="LXXXVIIIA"></COL> modo ac Burchardus exorditur <NOTE N="(305)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="LXXXVIIIC" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="LXXXVIIIC"></COL> P. II, lib. II, c. 1; Burch. lib. II, c. 1. P. II,
lib. III, c. 1-4; B. lib. XVI, c. 1-4. P. II, lib. IV,
c. 1-3; B. lib. VII, c. 1-3. Primus ejusdem partis
liber eodem modo incipit et explicit Burchardi liber,
qui ipsi respondet. P. II, lib. I, c. 1, c. 211-217. B.
lib. I, c. 1, 227-231.</NOTE> , et quamplurima
ex Pseudo-Ivonis Decreto habet <NOTE N="(306)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="LXXXVIIIC" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="LXXXVIIIC"></COL> Ut pateat quinam nexus hanc collectionem
inter et illas Burchardi et Pseudo-Ivonis existat,
primae partis librum quartum attente examinavimus,
et cum praedictis collectionibus contulimus. C. 1-3.
B. lib. III, c. 1; lib. I, c. 209; lib. III, c. 3. C. 4.
 <COL N="LXXXVIIID"></COL> Ps. I, p. III, c. 2. C. 5-32. B. lib. III, c. 81, 80, 82-84,
